  "goodToKnow": "Stapeln means to stack or pile up: Teller stapeln, and sich stapeln means to pile up: Die Post stapelt sich. Der Stapel is a stack. Figuratively, tiefstapeln means to understate or play things down, and hochstapeln means to pose as someone more important; der Hochstapler is a con man or impostor, like the fictional Felix Krull in Thomas Mann's novel. A ship launch is der Stapellauf. Regular: stapelte, gestapelt."
